  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises to adopt new business models, technology and techniques to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the results of COVID-19 Enterprise survey, conducted to collect data on situation of enterprises in Georgia and to better understand what type of assistance they need during the pandemic, the GEA developed a training programme to support small- and medium enterprises (SMEs), fostering the training on business continuity as an integral part of productivity improvements. The capacities of constituents on Business Continuity Planning (BCP) were strengthened by training 10 trainers on BCP, that will provide further trainings for enterprises. All training materials are available in Georgian language and are fully harmonized with the Georgian market. 
Online tool - six-step COVID-19 Business Continuity Plan &#x2013; aimed at supporting SMEs during the COVID-19 crisis and promoting productivity was developed and became accessible to all GEA members. This tool enables SMEs to assess the level of risk and vulnerability of business, and develop an effective risk and contingency system.  
The ILO OSH tools COVID-19 return to work (Prevention and Mitigation of COVID-19 at Work) is available to GEA members (in Georgian), complemented by the national report on OSH tools in Georgia, with specific instructions to companies. 100 companies were provided with training of trainers and detailed information regarding OSH tools COVID-19 return to work, to disseminate further information to enterprises.
 Technical support was provided by the ILO to develop an online tool - six-step COVID-19 Business Continuity Plan - to support SMEs during the COVID-19 crisis.  The ILO supported the translation of the training materials into Georgian language and its adaptation to the specifics of the Georgian market. The Training of trainers (ToTs) on the delivery of Business Continuity Planning was organized for 10 trainers from GEA and relevant government agencies (to be completed by end October).  
The on-line TOT on OSH tools COVID-19 return to work organized for 100 companies, providing detailed information regarding OSH tools, as well as the Action Checklist and instructions for the follow-up, which can be used for trainers to disseminate further information.</narrative>
   </description>
