  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.1. Increased capacity of member States to create an enabling environment for entrepreneurship and sustainable enterprises</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Georgian Employers&apos; Association (GEA) developed, with the support of ILO, and adopted a policy document on environment for sustainable enterprises. Based on GEA request, two pillars were targeted as the most important for enabling environment in Georgia: taxation and access to finance. Two sections specifically cover the impact of COVID on the Georgian economy. The document also includes the detailed explanation of digitalization as a new phenomena of the labour market and recommendations for coordinated policy measures on digitalization within the EESE pillars. The document was developed in close collaboration with social partners and provides policy recommendations for further development of enabling environment for businesses in Georgia.

With the support of the ILO, the Rapid Market Assessment and Value Chain Analysis was conducted for two selected sectors - food processing and agriculture, including the verification by the relevant stakeholders and developing recommendations for improving the environment for businesses in these economic sectors in Georgia. The ILO has provided policy advice to constituents to develop evidence based proposals for strengthening the business environment and to develop tripartite proposals for policy, regulatory and administrative changes to adapt to post-COVID recovery. Training was provided on the ILO OSH tools COVID-19 return to work (Prevention and Mitigation of COVID-19 at Work, etc.), taking into account specific needs of women-owned enterprises. 
The ILO commissioned the analysis of two selected sectors of the economy, identifying the key constraints to their performance conducted, including consultations with social partners. The ILO assisted the GEA in drafting intervention models in the target sectors. Special attention was given to collecting and documenting lessons learnt and good practices to facilitate replication in other countries as well as information sharing with all the national stakeholders.</narrative>
   </description>
